# Cursor Rules for dparker-dms Repository

## GitHub Configuration
- Always use and only use `davidparker-lv-bmth` as the GitHub user for this repository
- All commits, pull requests, and GitHub-related operations must use `davidparker-lv-bmth` as the user identifier

## Technology Stack Requirements

### Backend
- **Java 25 LTS** - All backend services must use Java 25
- **Spring Boot 3.4.x** - Framework version
- **Maven** - Build tool
- **JUnit 5** - Testing framework
- **Mockito** - Mocking framework

### Frontend
- **Angular 21** - Frontend framework (NOT Angular 25)
- **TypeScript** - Language
- **Angular Material 21** - UI component library
- **MSAL Angular** - Azure AD authentication

### Infrastructure & Deployment
- **Azure AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service)** - Container orchestration platform
- **Flux** - GitOps configuration management for Kubernetes
- **Istio** - Service mesh for microservices communication
- **Docker** - Containerization
- **Kubernetes** - Container orchestration

### Security & Compliance
- **Zero CVE Dependencies** - All dependencies must be free from known CVEs
- **OWASP Dependency Check** - Automated vulnerability scanning required
- **Regular Security Audits** - Dependencies must be scanned before each release
- **Dependency Updates** - Regular updates to patch vulnerabilities

## Code Quality Standards

### Unit Test Coverage
- **Minimum 90% code coverage** is required for all services
- All unit tests must be written using JUnit 5 and Mockito
- Tests must be stable, repeatable, and run in CI/CD pipelines
- All services must have comprehensive test suites covering:
  - Controllers (all endpoints)
  - Services (all business logic)
  - Repositories (data access layer)
  - Exception handlers
  - Security configurations
- Test coverage reports must be generated and verified before merging
- JaCoCo must be configured with 90% threshold enforcement

### Frontend Standards
- **WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance** is mandatory for all UI components
- All user interfaces must be:
  - Accessible to users with disabilities
  - Keyboard navigable
  - Screen reader compatible
  - High contrast compliant (4.5:1 ratio minimum)
  - Responsive and mobile-friendly
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide ARIA labels where appropriate
- Ensure focus indicators are visible
- Test with screen readers (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver)
- All forms must have proper labels and error messages
- Color must not be the only means of conveying information

### Security Standards
- **No CVE Vulnerabilities** - All dependencies must be scanned and free from CVEs
- **OWASP Dependency Check** - Must run in CI/CD pipeline
- **Dependency Updates** - Regular security updates required
- **Vulnerability Scanning** - Automated scanning before each build
- **Security Headers** - All services must include security headers
- **Input Validation** - All inputs must be validated
- **SQL Injection Prevention** - Use parameterized queries (JPA)
- **XSS Protection** - Sanitize all user inputs

### Infrastructure Standards
- **Azure AKS** - All services deployed to Azure Kubernetes Service
- **Flux GitOps** - Configuration managed via Flux for:
  - Kubernetes manifests
  - ConfigMaps
  - Secrets
  - Service configurations
- **Istio Service Mesh** - Required for:
  - Service-to-service communication
  - Traffic management
  - Security policies
  - Observability
  - mTLS between services
- **Container Security** - All containers must be scanned for vulnerabilities
- **Image Scanning** - Container images scanned before deployment

## Dependency Management

### CVE Prevention
- **OWASP Dependency Check Maven Plugin** - Required in all POMs
- **npm audit** - Required for frontend dependencies
- **Automated Scanning** - CI/CD must fail if CVEs detected
- **Regular Updates** - Dependencies updated monthly
- **Security Advisories** - Monitor and patch immediately
- **Dependency Whitelist** - Only approved dependencies allowed

### Version Management
- **Java 25 LTS** - Strict version requirement
- **Angular 21** - Strict version requirement (NOT 25)
- **Spring Boot 3.4.x** - Compatible with Java 25
- **Azure SDK** - Latest stable versions
- **Security Patches** - Applied immediately

## Deployment Standards

### Kubernetes
- **Azure AKS** - Primary deployment platform
- **Helm Charts** - Package management (if used)
- **Flux** - GitOps configuration management
- **Resource Limits** - All pods must have resource limits
- **Health Checks** - Liveness and readiness probes required
- **Service Discovery** - Kubernetes DNS for service-to-service communication

### Service Mesh (Istio)
- **mTLS** - Mutual TLS required between services
- **Traffic Policies** - Defined via Istio VirtualServices
- **Circuit Breakers** - Implemented via Istio
- **Retry Policies** - Configured via Istio
- **Rate Limiting** - Enforced via Istio
- **Observability** - Metrics, logs, traces via Istio

### GitOps (Flux)
- **Flux Controllers** - GitRepository, Kustomization, HelmRepository
- **Configuration as Code** - All K8s configs in Git
- **Automated Sync** - Flux automatically syncs from Git
- **Environment Separation** - Separate Flux namespaces per environment
- **Secret Management** - Flux with Sealed Secrets or External Secrets Operator

## Build & CI/CD Requirements

### Maven Builds
- **OWASP Dependency Check** - Must pass before build
- **JaCoCo Coverage** - Must meet 90% threshold
- **Tests** - All tests must pass
- **No CVEs** - Build fails if CVEs detected

### Frontend Builds
- **npm audit** - Must pass with no vulnerabilities
- **Angular 21** - Version must be exactly 21.x
- **TypeScript** - Strict mode enabled
- **Linting** - ESLint/Angular lint must pass

### CI/CD Pipeline
- **Dependency Scanning** - OWASP + npm audit
- **Test Execution** - All tests must pass
- **Coverage Verification** - 90% minimum
- **Security Scanning** - Container image scanning
- **Flux Sync** - Automated deployment via Flux
- **Istio Validation** - Service mesh policies validated

## Application Identifier

- All application identifiers must use `davidparker-lv-bmth` as specified
- Storage containers: `davidparker-lv-bmth-documents`
- Application role: `DMS.davidparker-lv-bmth`
- Key Vault secrets prefixed with `davidparker-lv-bmth-` where applicable

## Repository Structure Standards

### Multi-Repository Architecture
The DMS project is structured for standalone repositories. Each service and component will have its own GitHub repository:
- `dms-admin-service` - Administration service repository
- `dms-audit-service` - Audit logging service repository
- `dms-compliance-service` - Compliance service repository
- `dms-document-service` - Document management service repository
- `dms-llm-service` - LLM/AI service repository
- `dms-frontend-service` - Angular frontend repository
- `dms-core-service` - Shared library repository
- `dms-e2e-tests` - End-to-end test suite repository
- `dms-docs` - Documentation and reference configurations repository

### Folder Naming Conventions
- **Documentation**: `dms-docs/` (NOT `docs/`)
- **E2E Tests**: `dms-e2e-tests/` (NOT `e2e-tests/`)
- **Reference Configs**: `dms-docs/reference/` (clusters, flux-config, istio-config)
- **Dev Scripts**: `dms-docs/scripts/` (all development utilities)

### Docker Compose
- **docker-compose.yml** MUST be in the root directory
- MUST build and start all services for local development
- MUST include all required dependencies (PostgreSQL, Redis, etc.)
- MUST use service names matching repository names
- MUST configure proper health checks and dependencies

### Development Scripts and Utilities
- **ALL development scripts** (`.sh`, `.py`, etc.) MUST be stored in `dms-docs/scripts/`
- Service-specific scripts can remain in their service folders
- Shared utilities and helper scripts go in `dms-docs/scripts/`
- Scripts should be documented in `dms-docs/README.md`

## Documentation Standards

### Documentation Location
- **ALL documentation files** (except README.md files) MUST be created in the `dms-docs/` folder
- README.md files can remain in their respective folders (root, service folders, etc.)
- No documentation files (.md) should be created outside the `dms-docs/` folder except README.md files
- Reference configurations (clusters, flux-config, istio-config) MUST be in `dms-docs/reference/`

### Documentation Creation and Updates
- **BEFORE creating any new documentation file**, you MUST:
  1. First check if a document with the same or similar name already exists in the `dms-docs/` folder
  2. If a document exists, you MUST update the existing document instead of creating a new one
  3. When updating an existing document, you MUST add or update the metadata section at the top with:
     - GitHub username: `davidparker-lv-bmth`
     - Date and time stamp of the update in ISO 8601 format (e.g., `2024-01-18T13:32:00Z`)
  4. If no similar document exists, create the new document in the `dms-docs/` folder

### Documentation Metadata Format
When updating existing documentation, add or update the metadata section at the top of the file:

```markdown
---
Last Updated: 2024-01-18T13:32:00Z
Updated By: davidparker-lv-bmth
---
```

### Documentation File Naming
- Use descriptive, kebab-case names (e.g., `user-guide.md`, `architecture-overview.md`)
- Avoid generic names that might conflict with existing documents
- Check `dms-docs/` folder before creating to ensure no duplicates

### Reference Configurations
- Kubernetes cluster configs: `dms-docs/reference/clusters/`
- Flux GitOps configs: `dms-docs/reference/flux-config/`
- Istio service mesh configs: `dms-docs/reference/istio-config/`
- These are reference documents and should not be modified directly in the docs repo
- Service-specific deployments should copy and adapt these configs

